Description: Every speech-to-text engine says why it cannot dictate; Vibe's server starts at the press
 Three changes to the library as the edition ships it, each said to the person in one
 sentence, never only in the log.
 .
 An engine chosen that is not there is said, and no other engine is taken in its place:
 the manager no longer falls back to the first engine of an unordered table. The loader
 keeps why an engine cannot take a dictation (SpeechToTextEngineLoader::
 engineNotReadyReason): it is not installed; its program is missing (an engine skipped
 for its X-KTextAddons-RequiredExecutable names itself with X-KTextAddons-Engine and
 X-KTextAddons-EngineName, so the sentence names Vibe and vibe-server); or this version
 only lists it. With nothing chosen anywhere, the first engine that can take a
 dictation is used, in name order.
 .
 The Google and Whisper engines of 2.1.2 only log "Not implemented yet", also at
 2.3.0's tag for Google; 2.3.0's Whisper engine needs faster-whisper and ctranslate2 in
 a Python environment of its own, which Debian does not ship. Both stay listed, as
 upstream has them, with X-KTextAddons-NotAvailable in their metadata: the settings
 say "not available in this version" as soon as one is chosen (a message under the
 engine list), and so does a dictation asked of it.
 .
 The Vibe engine starts vibe-server when the person presses the dictation button, so
 the model loads while they speak, and sends the recording when they stop; the server
 is stopped when the answer is in, when the dictation is dropped, when the program
 quits, or when the recording cannot start (a microphone that does not open), and a
 server that fails while the person speaks is said at once and ends the capture. The
 manager gains cancel(): the capture stops, nothing is given, and the engine's work
 for the dictation ends with its plugin; it is called by Escape on the library's
 dictation button while it records, when the requester of the dictation is destroyed
 (its window closed), and when the application quits. A second dictation while Vibe
 still transcribes the first waits and says so. The engine logs the server's process
 number when it starts it and when it ends it.
 .
 Tests in the library's framework, with the stand-in vibe-server (a set model-load and
 answer time, and the times it started, was ready, was asked and was terminated): the
 engine through the plugin interface, the manager through its public interface, and
 the settings message.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
